{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>In the flame of fire.</b> In a flame of fire — the heart of the fire, as in ״לֵב הַשָּׁמַיִם״ (Deuteronomy 4), ״בְּלֵב הָאֵלָה״ (II Samuel 18). And do not wonder at the tav, for we have its parallel: ״מָה אֲמֻלָה לִבָּתֵךְ״ (Ezekiel 16)." "<b>Out of the midst of the thornbush.</b> And no other tree — because ״עִמּוֹ אָנֹכִי בְּצָרָה״ (Psalms 91:15)." "<b>Consumed.</b> Was consumed, as in ״לֹא עֻבַּד בָּהּ״ (Deuteronomy 21), ״אֲשֶׁר לֻקַּח מִשָּׁם״ (Genesis 3)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:21.759208045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}